Nausicaa directly depends on @earendil-works/pi-ai and @earendil-works/pi-tui
(MIT, https://github.com/earendil-works/pi). Model discovery, provider request
conversion, streaming, multimodal content types, and the terminal primitives
remain upstream responsibilities and are not reimplemented here.

Portions of src/tools/edit-diff.ts, src/tools/file-mutation-queue.ts,
src/tools/shell-output.ts, and src/tools/shell-process.ts are adapted from Pi
and Prime Agent. The @image operand, image MIME-detection flow, clipboard image
reader, and [image #N] marker logic are minimally adapted from Prime Agent's
coding-agent package as audited at commit
7787f07415d843b9a800f6a4720e0c739bd608e5. The semantic tool presentation
registry in src/cli/tool-renderers.ts minimally adapts that commit's
ToolExecutionComponent, Bash preview, and rich diff presentation behavior.
The thinkingRecap helper in src/cli/tui-components.ts minimally adapts
packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/components/assistant-message.ts
from the same Prime Agent commit
7787f07415d843b9a800f6a4720e0c739bd608e5.
Native clipboard access is provided by the optional
@mariozechner/clipboard 0.3.9 dependency (MIT). Nausicaa does not copy Prime's
daemon, RPC, inline-session serialization, IPython, or image resizing stack;
workspace policy, limits, persistence, and pi-ai integration are local glue.

